/api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR introduces a `forbidigo` linter rule to prohibit the use of `time.Sleep` throughout the codebase, replacing it with more appropriate synchronization patterns. The changes refactor test code to use `assert.EventuallyWithT` for polling/waiting patterns, replace small delays in race condition tests with `runtime.Gosched()` for yielding, and update production code to use proper backoff strategies or context-aware waiting.\n\nKey changes:\n- Added `forbidigo` linter configuration to block `time.Sleep` with guidance on appropriate alternatives\n- Refactored test files to use `assert.EventuallyWithT` for condition-based waiting patterns\n- Updated production code to use backoff strategies and context cancellation\n- Added `//nolint:forbidigo` directives with justifications for legitimate time-based waits (e.g., waiting for external service behaviors)\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 12 out of 13 changed files in this pull request and generated 3 comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| .golangci.yaml | Adds forbidigo linter configuration to block time.Sleep with context-specific guidance for alternatives |\r\n| integration/embedded_derp_test.go | Adds nolint directive with justification for intentional 30s delay to wait for DERP updater cycles |\r\n| integration/cli_test.go | Replaces time.Sleep with EventuallyWithT to poll for client stopped state |\r\n| integration/auth_oidc_test.go | Adds nolint directive for cache expiration wait (HEADSCALE_TUNING_REGISTER_CACHE_EXPIRATION) |\r\n| integration/auth_key_test.go | Adds nolint directives for Tailscale client non-HTTPS reconnection delays and replaces sleep with EventuallyWithT |\r\n| hscontrol/state/node_store_test.go | Replaces time.Sleep with EventuallyWithT for goroutine stabilization checks |\r\n| hscontrol/mapper/batcher_test.go | Extensive refactoring: replaces time.Sleep with EventuallyWithT, runtime.Gosched() for race testing |\r\n| hscontrol/derp/server/derp_server.go | Replaces time.Sleep with context-aware select statement using time.After for rate limiting |\r\n| hscontrol/db/node_test.go | Refactors ephemeral GC tests to use shorter timeouts, EventuallyWithT, and channel-based synchronization |\r\n| hscontrol/db/ephemeral_garbage_collector_test.go | Replaces time.Sleep with EventuallyWithT and runtime.Gosched(), removes math/rand usage |\r\n| hscontrol/auth_test.go | Removes time.Sleep delays for buffered channel operations, relying on channel buffering |\r\n| cmd/hi/cleanup.go | Refactors container removal retry logic to use cenkalti/backoff library with exponential backoff |\r\n| go.sum | Updates dependency checksums (removes outdated package versions) |\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/juanfont/headscale/new/main/.github/instructions?filename=*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.","commit_id":"899ccbe7441838d6a5802ef90eea015c46fd2041","state":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2946#pullrequestreview-3552672427","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/2946","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2946#pullrequestreview-3552672427"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/2946"}},"submitted_at":"2025-12-08T15:36:05Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T15:36:05Z","author_asso